  m_Name: Ending_Mountain
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Ending
  endingTitle: Mountain
  titleDA: "P\xE5 Bjerget"
  descriptionDA: "Pandaen er i bjergene, hvor vandet er knapt, og bambussen vokser
    langsomt. Her er der fredeligt, men der er langt mellem bambusskuddene, og pandaen
    m\xE5 bruge meget tid og energi p\xE5 at finde nok at spise. \n\nDet er ikke
    n\xF8dvendigvis en d\xE5rlig ting for pandaer at leve i bjergene. Om sommeren,
    n\xE5r varmen er moderat, trives de bedst heroppe. Om vinteren finder de mere
    bambus nede i dalene, og derfor rejser pandaer op og ned ad bjergene gennem \xE5ret.\n\nN\xE5r
    du g\xE5r i zoo st\xF8tter du pandaerne, de er med i et avls program af China
    Wildlife Conservation Association som er del i at sikre pandaens langsigtede
    overlevelse. Hvis du skal k\xF8be bambus produkter kan du selv kigge efter FSC-m\xE6rkede
    produkter som garantere at vigtige levesteder ikke er blevet \xF8delagt. "
  titleEN: On The Mountain
  descriptionEN: "The panda is high in the mountains, where water is scarce and bamboo
    grows slowly. It\u2019s peaceful, but the shoots are far apart, and finding enough
    food takes a lot of time and energy.\n\nLiving in the mountains isn\u2019t necessarily
    bad for pandas. They thrive best here in summer, when the heat is moderate. In
    winter they find more bamboo in the valleys, which is why they travel up and
    down the mountains through the year.\n\nWhen you visit the zoo, you support the
    pandas. They are part of a breeding program run by the China Wildlife Conservation
    Association, which helps secure the panda\u2019s long-term survival. When buying
    bamboo products, look for the FSC label, which guarantees that important habitats
    haven\u2019t been destroyed."
  endingImage: {fileID: 0}
